        "date": "2026-11-11T14:13:43Z"
      },
      "message": "docs(process): classify-effort - review fixes (placeholders, tie-break order, floor on the remainder)\n\n- The label commands use quoted LEVEL/REASON placeholders and a heredoc,\n  so nothing in them is read as a shell redirect or run as a command.\n- The table row decides; the questions only break ties, in a stated order.\n- The safety floor is restated for the remaining stage of an umbrella.\n- Smaller notes from the review: needs-research wording, research-shaped\n  work back in the max row, escalation kept apart from first\n  classification, the sweep prints before applying and says what its\n  query excludes; AGENTS.md says the skill never lowers a label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
